{
  "tema": 5929,
  "slug": "venzo-convenzo-c-z",
  "titulo": "-cer and -cir verbs: c > z in yo",
  "subtitulo": "Te convenzo. Ejerzo la medicina.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "In verbs ending in consonant + -cer/-cir (vencer, convencer, ejercer, torcer, esparcir), the c becomes z in the yo form of the present to keep the soft sound: venzo, convenzo, ejerzo. The other forms keep the c.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In Spanish, **c** sounds soft (like s) before **e** and **i**, but hard (like k) before **o**. In the **yo** form, **-o** would make it sound like k."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "So the spelling switches to **z**, which keeps the soft sound: **vencer → venzo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "This happens when a **consonant** comes before **-cer** or **-cir**. **Cocer** is the odd one out: vowel before **-cer**, but still **cuezo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Infinitive",
            "yo",
            "tú"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "vencer _to beat_",
              "**venzo**",
              "vences"
            ],
            [
              "convencer _to convince_",
              "**convenzo**",
              "convences"
            ],
            [
              "ejercer _to practice (a profession)_",
              "**ejerzo**",
              "ejerces"
            ],
            [
              "torcer _to twist_",
              "**tuerzo**",
              "tuerces"
            ],
            [
              "esparcir _to scatter_",
              "**esparzo**",
              "esparces"
            ],
            [
              "cocer _to cook, boil_",
              "**cuezo**",
              "cueces"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Only **yo** changes. **Tú, él, nosotros, ellos** keep the **c**: **convences, convence, convencemos, convencen**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Torcer** and **cocer** also change **o > ue** like other stem-changers: **tuerzo, tuerces… torcemos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Don't mix it up with **vowel** + **-cer/-cir**, which takes **zc**: **conocer → conozco**, **conducir → conduzco**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Siempre ==venzo== a mi hermano en el jiu-jitsu.",
              "en": "I always beat my brother at jiu-jitsu."
            },
            {
              "es": "Si no quieres venir, yo te ==convenzo==.",
              "en": "If you don't want to come, I'll convince you."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ejerzo== la medicina en Tijuana.",
              "en": "I practice medicine in Tijuana."
            },
            {
              "es": "Siempre me ==tuerzo== el tobillo en la arena.",
              "en": "I always twist my ankle in the sand."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Cuezo== los frijoles en la olla de presión.",
              "en": "I cook the beans in the pressure cooker."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Esparzo== las semillas de cilantro en el huerto.",
              "en": "I scatter the cilantro seeds in the garden."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tú siempre me ==convences==.",
              "en": "You always convince me."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
